  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Effektivitets revision AECF</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Efficiency Audit of AECF</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Africa Enterprice Challenge Fund (AECF) &#xe4;r en sk. &#x2019;Challenge Fund&#x2019; som initierats av multilaterala och bilaterala givare f&#xf6;r att stimulera entrepren&#xf6;rer inom den privata sektorn i Afrika. Fonden har till dags dato mobiliserat ca MUSD 244 och har f&#xf6;rnybar energi och jordbruk som sina huvudsakliga fokus omr&#xe5;den.

Den planerade effektivitetsrevisionen syftar till att bed&#xf6;ma om AECFs interna f&#xf6;rvaltnings- och kontrollsystem &#xe4;r tillr&#xe4;ckliga f&#xf6;r att s&#xe4;kerst&#xe4;lla kvalitet och noggrannhet i rapporteringen. Revisionen ska bed&#xf6;ma om AECF har l&#xe4;mpliga system och rutiner f&#xf6;r att hantera sin verksamhet f&#xf6;r att uppn&#xe5; de operativa m&#xe5;len . Granskningen kommer ocks&#xe5; att vara ett viktigt bidrag i givarnas utarbetande av ev nya avtal. Revisions ska f&#xf6;resl&#xe5; &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder f&#xf6;r att hantera identifierade brister.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The AECF is a US$ 244m challenge fund capitalized by multilateral and bilateral donors (the AECF donors) to stimulate private sector entrepreneurs in Africa to innovate and find profitable ways of improving access to markets and the way markets function for the poor, particularly in rural areas.

The efficiency audit aims at assessing whether the Africa Enterprise Challenge Fund (AECF) internal management and control systems are adequate to ensure quality and accuracy of narrative and financial reports. At an overall level, the aim is to assess whether the AECF has appropriate systems and routines for managing its activities to achieve the operational goals. The audit will also be an important input in addressing the due diligence requirements of the donors, nessesary in the transfer of of assignments of donor agreements to the new entity. The efficiency audit is expected to find eventual weaknesses and to suggest actions to address these.</narrative>
  </description>
